  "assumptions": [
   "Three planet gears, the usual choice for load sharing and balance.",
   "Input and output shafts are coaxial and leave the housing at opposite ends, each running on two deep-groove ball bearings in the housing.",
   "Open bearing caps where each shaft leaves the housing, sealed against oil.",
   "No sizes were given, so module, teeth, shaft diameters and bearings are left for standard sizing.",
   "Gears, shafts and pins in alloy steel; housing and cover in cast iron."
  ],
  "questions": [],
  "answers": {
   "planet_count": "3",
   "material_housing": "Cast iron"
  },
  "notes": [
   "Ring gear: 90 internal teeth (z_ring = z_sun + 2 z_planet = 30 + 2 x 30), so the sun and the ring are coaxial.",
   "Planet bearing: 6004 (Ø20 x Ø42 x 12) instead, because 6204 (OD 47) left a rim of 4 mm = 2 m under the planet's Ø55 root, less than 2.7 m.",
   "Planet bearing 6004: rim (Ø55 root - Ø42) / 2 = 6.5 mm = 3.25 m under the planet teeth, at least 2.7 m (ISO 6336-3 / AGMA 2001-D04: rim at least 1.2 tooth depths, 1.2 x 2.25 m (verify)).",
   "Planet bearing is not carried by Housing base in a planetary set: that joint is left out (it runs on its own axis in the set).",
   "Cover bolts: 4, one per hole the layout made for them (6 were planned)."
  ],
  "source": "intent"
 }
